1. Adequate ingress and egress to a major street is ensured;
2. They are provided with adequate, paved off-street parking areas;
3. The buildings are placed not less than 30 feet from street lines and not less than 25 feet from property lines; and
4. Adequate provisions are made for maintaining a planted buffer strip along adjoining property lines.
i) Bed and breakfast when operated without a restaurant and located within the downtown historic district of the city, that has been entered in the National Register of Historic Places.

