1207:
The manufactured home district is established to provide for the placement of manufactured home subdivisions and manufactured home parks in suitable areas of the city. In promoting the general purpose of the ordinance, the specific intent of this section is:
a) To require adequate space and facilities for healthful living conditions for occupants of such manufactured home parks and manufactured home subdivisions;
b) To require all such districts to have access to a paved roadway for easy accessibility;
c) To ensure that suitable water and sewer facilities will be provided in accordance with all applicable state and county health regulations and statutes; and
d) To encourage the development of manufactured home parks for long-term residential use rather than transient travel trailer use.
These regulations shall govern the design and improvement of manufactured home parks and subdivisions within the city limits.

